{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"734864101892685976","content":"Web kneels in front of the graves and begins to speak a prayer in Druidic. ||Wild forces, it has been many a moon since the deaths of James Gilligan Pierce and Katrina Logan Caldwell, but I ask that their passing not be in vain. Let their bodies return to the earth and nourish it, as it once nourished them. Let the words of their tongues and the wisdom of their years not be so easily forgotten. Let their son Castor be strong. Let him live long, grow into the might of his years, and have a peaceful, earned passage. May these bodies serve as a reminder of the ties of love, and of the inevitable truth. We will all be claimed in the end. ||\nWeb takes a small bundle of herbs, plants, and fungus and lays it on the grave. \n||Let these pieces of nature keep their memories fresh, so that they will still live on in peace||\nWeb stands up and goes to castor. \"I have done my duty. Their deaths will be of use, will mean something\"","created_at":"2020-07-22T07:05:42.119000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"735392110714552350","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
